## Important Security Takeaways

- A professional-looking message is not automatically trustworthy.
- Matching displayed link text and destination is useful, but it does not guarantee that a link is safe.
- Never share an OTP with another person or enter it on an untrusted website.
- If an unexpected OTP arrives, do not approve or share it. Check the account through its official app or website.
- Verify suspicious requests independently before taking action.

## Conclusion

This task taught me that phishing defence is not just about spotting suspicious grammar or links. It also requires slowing down, verifying the sender and destination, and following consistent security habits even when a message looks genuine.
